; DECnet node names, one node per line:
;
;   NAME  ADDRESS  [keyword ...]
;
; NAME           node name, as used in DN:NAME and by the dn tools
; ADDRESS        area.node (area 1-63, node 1-1023)
;
; Keywords after the address, in any order:
; USER name      user name for files on the node (omit: none)
; PASSWORD word  password for that user (omit: none)
; NOBLOCK        don't offer DAP blocking (some servers need it)
; PURGE          DN: deletes older VMS versions of a file after
;                writing it; without it they are kept
; SHOW           node appears as a drawer in DN:; if no node has
;                SHOW, all nodes appear. Others stay reachable by
;                name (DN:NAME).
;
; Lines starting with ";" are comments. dnnodes FROM=node UPDATE
; appends nodes that another node knows. Used by decnet.library
; (DnNodeAddr) and DN:.
;
; This file is ENVARC:DECnet/nodes; it is copied to ENV:DECnet/nodes
; at boot. After editing it, copy it to ENV:DECnet/nodes as well (or
; reboot). DN: and the dn tools read the copy in ENV:.
